  "note": "Triennial urban council election of May 1961. No newspaper report has been found; the Belfast and Ulster Directory 1962 lists the nine members of the council. Nine members printed (chairman Robert A. Linton, J.P.; vice-chairman Edward M'Gonigle, J.P.). Directory list, not an election report: the directory prints the council's membership as it stood when the edition was compiled (late in the year after the election). It does not say whether members were returned at a poll or unopposed, and cannot show co-options made between the election and compilation. No votes."
